# bat configuration — one CLI argument per line.
#
# Kanagawa is not built into bat, so the theme is vendored as
# themes/kanagawa-dragon.tmTheme. bat only picks a theme file up from a
# compiled cache, so after a fresh `./install.sh bat` (or any edit to it) run:
#
#     bat cache --build
#
# `bat --list-themes` should then show `kanagawa-dragon`. Note bat names a
# *user* theme after its filename, not the `name` key inside the plist, and a
# wrong value is silent — bat falls back to its built-in Monokai default and
# prints orange rather than erroring. Verify after any rename.
#
# The file is upstream's extras/tmTheme/kanagawa.tmTheme with every colour
# swapped Wave -> Dragon, paired by the role each fills in kanagawa.nvim's
# themes.lua. Upstream only ships a Wave tmTheme, and using it directly would
# have left bat purple-tinted while everything else is warm. The scope
# coverage and structure are untouched. Palette: see docs/palette.md.

--theme="kanagawa-dragon"

# Line numbers, git modification markers and a header per file, but no grid.
--style="numbers,changes,header"

# Only page when the output doesn't fit; keep colors and let bat's default
# less flags through.
--paging=auto
